# Michelle, intro (figure 82.1)
# A held C on top over a chromatic inner line F E Eb D Db C, all on an f-minor "envelope" until
# the V (a bare open fifth on C) in bar 4. Notes in a bar get equal shares (the typed spacing is
# not a reliable guide to rhythm).
# Pollack's footnote: iv 6/5 here can alternately be parsed as vi 4/3 (D-flat) by virtue of the F
# in the bass (the low F he says enters at the start of bar 3; he doesn't type it in the chart).
meter 4/4
key f

system
voice "Melody"       | C5 | - |
voice "Inner line"   | F4 E4 | Eb4 D4 |
chords "Chords"      | f{i} | - |

system
voice "Melody"       | - C5 Bb4 Ab4 | C5 |
voice "Inner line"   | Db4 | C4 |
chords "Chords"      | b-flat{iv 6/5 **} | C{V} |
caption ** iv 6/5 here can be alternately parsed as vi 4/3 (D-flat) by virtue of the F in the bass
